summary:
  The stopgap branch goes back to erasing the 10-minute lookup lock, so
  a backup address that buffers and then dies rides the search-and-
  notify ring with no backoff at all.

history:
  The lock erasure was written in good faith — "the audition WORKED, let
  a stop-and-replay heal again right away" — and the 2026-08-20 review
  showed its other face: a flapping cross-domain backup re-entered the
  ladder seconds after every death, each round with a fresh notification,
  and the exponential backoff never engaged because the commit kept
  resetting the very lock the backoff leaned on. The user's own press
  releases the lock in refreshServer now; the commit never does. This
  mutant puts the erasure back.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          if (HealLogic.commitVerdict(byUuid, oldBase,
                                      _baseDomain(_hostOf(newUrl)), exact) !== "permanent") {

replace:
          if (HealLogic.commitVerdict(byUuid, oldBase,
              _baseDomain(_hostOf(newUrl)), exact) !== "permanent") { delete _healTried[oldUrl];

expect:
  Killed by test_invariants.py
  test_the_heal_commit_gate_is_the_tested_one_and_the_stopgap_keeps_the_lock:
  "delete _healTried" reappears inside the gate's stopgap stretch.
  Line-neutral — main.qml sits under the line ratchet, and a growing
  mutant would be "killed" by the size lock instead of the real guard.
